				el('span', { class: 'ds-pv-url-bar' }, mark(s.logo, s.brand[0], undefined, 'ds-pv-logo'), el('span', { class: 'ds-pv-ellipsis' }, el('span', { class: 'ds-pv-sub' }, s.page.domain), s.page.path)),
			),
		)
		const tiles = BOARD_TILES.slice(1).map((t, i) => el('div', { class: 'ds-pv-tile', style: tileStyle(t) }, pic(s.tiles[i], n + i + 1, {}, s.tiles[i] ?? {})))
		const avatars = [0, 1].map((i) => el('div', { class: 'ds-pv-avatar', style: `--cx: ${BOARD_AVATAR.x[i]}; --cy: ${BOARD_AVATAR.y}; --d: ${BOARD_AVATAR.d}` }, pic(s.creators[i]?.avatar, n + i + 4)))
		const chips = [0, 1].map((i) => el('span', { class: 'ds-pv-handle-chip', style: `--cx: ${BOARD_AVATAR.x[i]}; --edge: ${BOARD_AVATAR.y + BOARD_AVATAR.d / 2}` }, s.creators[i]?.handle ?? ''))
		const scene = el('div', { class: 'ds-pv-scene', style: `visibility: ${n === 0 ? 'visible' : 'hidden'}` }, page, tiles, avatars.map((a, i) => [a, chips[i]]))
		return { scene, tiles: [page, ...tiles], avatars, chips }
	})
	const view = el('div', { class: 'ds-pv-boardview' }, scenes.map((s) => s.scene))
	const canvas = el('div', { class: 'ds-pv-canvas', 'aria-hidden': 'true' }, view)
	const node = el('div', { class: 'ds-pv-board' }, canvas,
		el('div', { class: 'ds-pv-sr' }, d.scenes.map((s) => el('p', {}, `${s.brand}: ${s.page.ads.replace('point here', 'point to')} ${s.page.domain}${s.page.path}. Creators it works with: ${s.creators.map((c) => c.handle).join(' and ')}.`))),
	)
	const loop = BOARD_SCENE * scenes.length
	return {
		node,
		start(root) {
			let u = 1
			const measure = () => (u = Math.max(node.clientWidth, node.clientHeight) / BOARD_VIEW)
			let shown = 0
			let drawn = -1
			const draw = (f: number) => {
				if (f === drawn) return
				drawn = f
				const n = Math.floor(f / BOARD_SCENE) % scenes.length
				const k = f - Math.floor(f / BOARD_SCENE) * BOARD_SCENE
				if (n !== shown) {
					scenes[shown].scene.style.visibility = 'hidden'
					scenes[n].scene.style.visibility = 'visible'
					shown = n
				}
				view.style.transform = `scale(${boardZoomAt(k)})`
				const p = scenes[n]
				p.tiles.forEach((t, i) => {
					const v = boardTileAt(i, k)
					t.style.opacity = String(v.opacity)
					t.style.transform = v.scale < 1 ? `scale(${v.scale})` : ''
				})
				for (let i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
					const a = boardAvatarAt(i, k)
					p.avatars[i].style.opacity = String(a.opacity)
					p.avatars[i].style.transform = `scale(${a.scale})`
					const c = boardChipAt(i, k)
					p.chips[i].style.opacity = String(c.opacity)
					p.chips[i].style.transform = `translate(-50%, ${(c.dy * u).toFixed(2)}px)`
				}
			}
			const reduce = window.matchMedia(REDUCED)
			let raf = 0
			let onScreen = false
			let last = 0
			let clock = BOARD_STILL * BOARD_STEP
			let owed = pacing(root).first
			const frame = () => (clock / BOARD_STEP) % loop
			const tick = (now: number) => {
				const dt = last ? Math.min(now - last, 100) : 0
				last = now
				if (owed > 0) owed -= dt
				else clock += dt
				draw(frame())
				raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick)
			}
			const update = () => {
				cancelAnimationFrame(raf)
				raf = 0
				last = 0
				if (reduce.matches) return draw(BOARD_STILL)
				draw(frame())
				if (onScreen && document.visibilityState === 'visible') raf = requestAnimationFrame(tick)
			}
			const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
				onScreen = entries[entries.length - 1].isIntersecting
				update()
			}, { threshold: 0.25 })
			const ro = new ResizeObserver(() => {
				measure()
				const f = drawn
				drawn = -1
				if (f >= 0) draw(f)
			})
			measure()
			io.observe(root)
			ro.observe(node)
			document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', update)
			reduce.addEventListener('change', update)
			update()
			return () => {
				cancelAnimationFrame(raf)
				io.disconnect()
				ro.disconnect()
				document.removeEventListener('visibilitychange', update)
				reduce.removeEventListener('change', update)
			}
		},
	}
}

function build(kind: ProductVisualKind, data: unknown): Built {
	switch (kind) {
		case 'brand-record':
		case 'creative-record':
		case 'page-record':
		case 'creator-record':
		case 'tagged-record':
			return record(kind, data as RecordData)
		case 'comment-thread':
			return thread(data as ThreadData)
		case 'add-account':
		case 'add-creator':
			return add(data as AddData)
		case 'comment-themes':
			return themes(data as ThemesData)
		case 'creator-filters':
			return filters(data as FiltersData)
		case 'filter-narrow':
		case 'posts-narrow':
			return narrow(data as NarrowData)
		case 'collabs-timeline':
		case 'tagged-timeline':
			return timeline(data as TimelineData)
		case 'media-mix':
		case 'campaigns':
		case 'pages-switch':
			return sheet(data as SheetData)
		case 'links-board':
			return board(data as BoardData)
		case 'patterns-switch':
			return patterns(data as PatternsData)
		default:
			return { node: el('div', { class: 'ds-pv-root' }), start: noop() }
	}
}

export interface MountProductVisualOptions<K extends ProductVisualKind = ProductVisualKind> {
	kind: K
	/** The kind's data; its Acme default when left out. */
	data?: ProductVisualDataMap[K]
	/** Which of the four ASCII field positions the stage takes (a product page alternates them by row), or false for none. */
	texture?: number | false
}

/** Builds the visual inside `stage` (the element carrying the `ds-pv` stage class) and starts its loop. Returns the
 * function that stops the loop and removes what it built. */
export function mountProductVisual<K extends ProductVisualKind>(stage: HTMLElement, { kind, data, texture = 0 }: MountProductVisualOptions<K>): () => void {
	const built = build(kind, data ?? productVisualDefaults[kind] ?? productVisualDefaults['brand-record'])
	const added: Node[] = []
	if (texture !== false) {
		const ascii = el('span', { class: 'ds-pv-ascii', 'aria-hidden': 'true', style: `--pv-ascii-at: ${productVisualAsciiAt[Math.abs(Math.trunc(texture)) % productVisualAsciiAt.length]}` })
		ascii.style.setProperty('--pv-ascii', `url("${ASCII_TEXTURE}")`)
		added.push(ascii)
	}
	added.push(built.node)
	added.forEach((n) => stage.appendChild(n))
	const stop = built.start(stage)
	return () => {
		stop()
		added.forEach((n) => n.parentNode?.removeChild(n))
	}
}

// The product visuals' data: one shape per family of visual and the defaults (Acme), shared by both flavors. The site's
// own visuals (pages/Products/visuals and v2/V2Features LinksBoard and PatternsSwitch) show real brands, creators and
// their pictures; these defaults keep the copy's shape with Acme and invented people, and leave every picture out, so
// each slot draws a neutral shape. Pass your own pictures (`picture`, `avatar`, `logo`, `src`) where you may show them.

import type { ImageSlot } from '@/lib/image'

export type ProductVisualKind =
	| 'brand-record'
	| 'creative-record'
	| 'page-record'
	| 'creator-record'
	| 'tagged-record'
	| 'comment-thread'
	| 'add-account'
	| 'add-creator'
	| 'comment-themes'
	| 'creator-filters'
	| 'filter-narrow'
	| 'posts-narrow'
	| 'collabs-timeline'
	| 'tagged-timeline'
	| 'media-mix'
	| 'campaigns'
	| 'pages-switch'
	| 'links-board'
	| 'patterns-switch'

export const productVisualKinds: ProductVisualKind[] = ['brand-record', 'creative-record', 'page-record', 'creator-record', 'tagged-record', 'comment-thread', 'add-account', 'add-creator', 'comment-themes', 'creator-filters', 'filter-narrow', 'posts-narrow', 'collabs-timeline', 'tagged-timeline', 'media-mix', 'campaigns', 'pages-switch', 'links-board', 'patterns-switch']

/** A record panel beside a picture, cycling through its sets (brand, creative, page, creator and tagged records). */
export interface RecordSet {
	/** The picture beside the panel (4:5): a src or { src, alt, fit, position }. A neutral shape when left out. */
	picture?: string | ImageSlot
	/** The panel's first line: a brand, a page or a person. */
	name: string
	/** The line under it: a handle, a domain or what the picture is. */
	sub: string
	/** The round mark before the name: an image, or the initial on White when there is none. */
	mark?: { src?: string; initial?: string }
	/** One value per label, in order. */
	values: string[]
}
export interface RecordData {
	labels: string[]
	sets: RecordSet[]
	/** Read by screen readers in place of the panel. */
	summary?: string
}

/** A post with three of its comments (comment-thread). */
export interface ThreadComment {
	handle: string
	likes: string
	text: string
	avatar?: string
}
export interface ThreadData {
	/** The account the posts are from. */
	handle: string
	sets: { picture?: string | ImageSlot; meta: string; comments: ThreadComment[] }[]
	summary?: string
}

/** Adding an account by its handles: added, indexing, ready (add-account, add-creator). */
export interface AddData {
	title: string
	/** The note opposite the title ("Free"). */
	free: string
	/** What was typed: a website, a handle. */
	inputs: string[]
	/** The status steps; the last is where the loop rests. */
	steps: string[]
	account: { name: string; initial: string; avatar?: string; category: string; followers: string }
	summary?: string
}

/** Comments sorted into themes, one theme at a time (comment-themes). */
export interface ThemesData {
	title: string
	themes: { label: string; share: string; comments: { handle: string; text: string; avatar?: string }[] }[]
	summary?: string
}

/** A creator search narrowed by filters (creator-filters). `step` is when a filter turns on (0: never), `out` when a
 * row leaves (0: never). */
export interface FiltersData {
	query: string
	filters: { label: string; value: string; step: number }[]
	rows: { handle: string; initial: string; avatar?: string; city: string; followers: string; out: number }[]
	summary?: string
}

/** A search narrowed by three filters over a grid of eight results (filter-narrow, posts-narrow). A tile dims at
 * step `out` (0: it stays). */
export interface NarrowData {
	query: string
	filters: string[]
	/** The result count at each step: before any filter, then after each. */
	counts: string[]
	tiles: (ImageSlot & { out: number })[]
	summary?: string
}

/** People ranked by posts with a brand, each with their run of posts on a time axis, filtered by window
 * (collabs-timeline, tagged-timeline). Dates are ISO days. */
export interface TimelineData {
	brand: { name: string; mark?: string }
	title: string
	/** Today, so dates in this year drop their year. */
	today: string
	axis: { from: string; to: string; labels: string[] }
	/** The windows; `from` null for all time. The loop rests on the second. */
	windows: { label: string; from: string | null }[]
	rows: { name: string; picture?: string | ImageSlot; first: string; latest: string; posts: string }[]
	summary?: string
}

/** A ranked sheet with a two-way switch: rows move, leave or change values with the view (media-mix, campaigns,
 * pages-switch). `at` is each row's place per view (null: not in that view); `fill` its share bar per view (0 to 1). */
export interface SheetData {
	brand: { name: string; logo?: string; note: string }
	views: string[]
	/** The switch's accessible name. */
	switchLabel: string
	rows: { key: string; picture?: string | ImageSlot; name: string; tag?: string; values: string[]; fill?: number[]; at: (number | null)[]; muted?: boolean }[]
	/** One per view, read by screen readers. */
	summary?: string[]
}

/** A board of a brand's landing page, its ads and two creators, building and clearing scene after scene
 * (links-board). Each scene takes eight tiles after the page. */
export interface BoardScene {
	brand: string
	logo?: string
	page: ImageSlot & { y?: number; domain: string; path: string; ads: string }
	tiles: (ImageSlot & { x?: number; y?: number; zoom?: number })[]
	creators: { handle: string; avatar?: string | ImageSlot }[]
}
export interface BoardData {
	scenes: BoardScene[]
}

/** A brand's top hooks, angles and personas as share bars over three ads, the top ad in focus (patterns-switch).
 * `top` lists the ads (by index) in focus for a view. */
export interface PatternsData {
	brand: string
	logo?: string
	window: string
	ads: (ImageSlot & { x?: number })[]
	views: { label: string; rows: { name: string; share: number }[]; top: number[] }[]
}

export interface ProductVisualDataMap {
	'brand-record': RecordData
	'creative-record': RecordData
	'page-record': RecordData
	'creator-record': RecordData
	'tagged-record': RecordData
	'comment-thread': ThreadData
	'add-account': AddData
	'add-creator': AddData
	'comment-themes': ThemesData
	'creator-filters': FiltersData
	'filter-narrow': NarrowData
	'posts-narrow': NarrowData
	'collabs-timeline': TimelineData
	'tagged-timeline': TimelineData
	'media-mix': SheetData
	campaigns: SheetData
	'pages-switch': SheetData
	'links-board': BoardData
	'patterns-switch': PatternsData
}

